-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, four power armors (printed 146-156): Sea Demon, Silent Shadow, Storm Hammer, Thunder Hound
-- 4 vehicle rows, with 36 locations and 14 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~313-northern-gun-2-power-armor-h.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-nx14-sea-demon', 'Sea Demon Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 40 mph (64 km) maximum, 50 mph (80 km) with the hydro-jet pack taken off, at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) high or across unassisted; jet-assisted, 120 ft (36.6 m) high and 300 ft (91.4 m) across without flight, or a dive 300 ft (91.4 m) down into water in 4 seconds. From the water it can spring as high as 120 ft (36.6 m) onto a deck, dock or shore.', 'None. After a leap it can hold a hover for 1D4 melee rounds (15 to 60 seconds) before it wobbles and drifts down.', 'Hydro-jet pack: 50 mph (80 km/43 knots) on the surface, prone, kneeling, standing or on skis or a board; 30 mph (48 km/26 knots) submerged. Dolphin-style leaping in and out of the water raises surface speed to 60 mph (96 km). Swims 8 mph (13 km/7 knots) without the jets; walks the bottom at 5 mph (8 km/4.3 knots). Maximum depth 3,000 ft (914 m).', 'Height 6.6-7.6 ft (2 to 2.3 m); width 4 ft (1.2 m) fin to fin; length 4 ft (1.2 m) with the hydro-jet pack, 3 ft 4 in (1 m) without. The cannon is 6 ft (1.8 m) long.', '582 lbs (262 kg); the cannon adds 198 lbs (89 kg)', 190, 1, NULL, 985000, '1.3 million credits nuclear, 985,000 Solid Oxide; the lowest is stored. No electric battery version. The cannon comes only with the suit. Silver plating the cannon''s Vibro-Bayonet is 6,000 more (gear row ng-nx14-sea-demon-bayonet-silver-plating) and the forearm Vibro-Blade 2,000 more (gear row ng-nx14-sea-demon-blade-silver-plating).', 'Model Type: NG-NX14. Class: Amphibious Infantry Assault Suit. A bulky deep-water suit released about eighteen months ago by Ralph Larjara, Toby Heck and B.M. Mumah for sailors, whalers and sea-monster hunters, and since taken up by marines, privateers and pirates for boarding ships. Its builders gave it a devil''s face with big curled ram''s horns and stingray-style fins over the hydro-jets. Its jets drive it through and over the waves and can fling it out of the sea into a hover or straight onto a ship''s deck, which makes it a terror for raids and surprise attacks; a few suits racing alongside a vessel often persuade an untrained crew to give up. Losing one or both fin-wings cuts water speed and leaping by 10% and limits a hover to one melee round. Robot P.S. 28. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 10 year average life; Solid Oxide priced. Handheld extras: any side arm, Vibro-Knife, Neural Mace, shotgun, grenades, flares or anti-monster gear, held in belt pouches and holsters (up to two belts) or a bag; the thrusters leave no room for a backpack. UEL (2, one under plating in each forearm): a cable and E-Clip connector giving any E-Clip weapon unlimited payload. Hand to hand per Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352), Robot P.S. 28: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), head butt 1D4, head butt with horns 1D6, gore with horns 2D4 (best on far bigger foes), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Cat-like landings: thrusters set it down safely, or into water, from as high as 300 ft (91.4 m), half that with the main back thrusters gone; from 300 to 600 ft (183 m) roll 1D20, on 1-10 the suit takes 4D6 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions, on 11-20 no harm or delay; higher drops do 2D6x10 M.D. to the suit, 6D6 S.D.C./Hit Points to the wearer and stun him 1D4 melee rounds. Features beyond the standard: two simple helmet cameras storing 96 hours of video and 4,000 stills; a mouthpiece loudspeaker with language translator and 20-voice modulator; passive nightvision (1,600 ft/488 m) with ultraviolet vision.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.146-148'),
  ('ng-uelx49-silent-shadow', 'Silent Shadow Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running (wings folded): 70 mph (112 km) maximum, reached from a standstill in one melee round, at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) high and 20 ft (6.1 m) across unassisted, doubled with the booster jets; a wing-assisted gliding leap reaches 130 ft (39.6 m) high and 300 ft (91.4 m) across without true flight.', 'Limited: a glider kept up by small hover jets, unable to hover in place, circling on air currents like a hawk. Usually 40 mph (64 km) or less; up to 120 mph (192 km) in a strong wind or diving from 100 ft (30.5 m) or higher, 240 mph (384 km) diving in from an aircraft above 10,000 ft (3,048 m). Flights normally last 30-60 minutes, three hours at most with steady wind. Best sustained altitude 2,000 ft (610 m); usually flown at 20-500 ft (6.1 to 152 m), as low as 2 ft (0.6 m). It can glide down and land safely from any height.', 'Not built for water; swims or walks the bottom at 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots), at 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Maximum depth 1,000 ft (305 m).', 'Man-sized: height 6-7.6 ft (1.8 to 2.3 m); width 3-4 ft (0.9 to 1.2 m) with wings down, 15 ft (4.6 m) at full spread; length 2-3 ft (0.6 to 0.9 m), all by the buyer''s size', '279 lbs (126 kg)', 190, 1, NULL, 1000000, '1.4 million credits nuclear, 1 million Solid Oxide; the lowest is stored. No electric battery version, the UEL drawing too much power. An extra thigh UEL is 160,000 more (gear row ng-uelx49-thigh-uel).', 'Model Type: NG-UELX49. Class: Strategic Flying Espionage Assault Suit with UEL system. Built by the Fillinger Team (Michael Reagin, Lorne Wheeler, Carl Gleba and Michael Wilson) alongside the Night Reaper''s designers, so the two suits can share spying, sabotage and infiltration work: the Night Reaper is the light stealth suit, this the heavier one for commando raids, surprise strikes, rescues and sabotage, border and coastal patrols, gliding from one ship onto another, night raids and diversions (a favorite is a few Silent Shadows firebombing one corner of a target while others work quietly elsewhere). Painted black with a lowered heat signature, it glides on big bat-like wings with vents and small hidden hover jets for lift and turns rather than loud thrusters, so it comes in silently and low, under most radar. NG cannot match Naruni camouflage, so it relies on an experimental radar trick instead (below). With little built-in firepower it depends on striking first and on handheld UEL-powered weapons; a rifle rides in a housing behind one shoulder, and grenades or firebombs in a shoulder bag or belt pouches can be dropped with fair accuracy from 50 ft (15.2 m) or less. Its wings are fragile in flight: losing one sends it spiralling to the ground, unable to glide again until the wing is replaced, and fast fighters such as the SAMAS, Triax Predator or NG Red Hawk can overwhelm it, so it is best used for scouting, hit and run attacks and diversions. Folded tight against the back on landing, the wings are hard to see or hit. With the Night Reaper it is gaining a name as a ninja among power armors. Robot P.S. 26. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 10 year average life; Solid Oxide priced. UEL (2, one under plating in each forearm): a cable and E-Clip connector that powers a weapon of up to 1D6x10 M.D. an attack. Hand to hand per Basic and Flying Power Armor Combat (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352), Robot P.S. 26: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks), flying power punch 3D6 (three attacks; no extra for two fists), flying leap kick 3D8 (three attacks), flying body block 3D8 (two attacks) with a 01-68% chance of knocking down a foe under 11 ft (3.4 m) and one ton, who loses initiative and one melee attack. Features beyond the standard: two simple helmet cameras storing 96 hours of video and 4,000 stills; helmet multi-optics with passive nightvision and infrared (1,600 ft/488 m each), ultraviolet (400 ft/122 m), binocular telescopic sight (2 miles/3.2 km) and x12 macro; a mouthpiece loudspeaker with language translator and 20-voice modulator; and the Stealth RADAR package, which answers incoming radar with false returns, imposing -60% on enemy Sensory Equipment rolls to spot it and other hostile flyers. On a failed roll it is taken for clutter and ignored; on a success roll percentile: 01-35 recognized as enemy power armor, perhaps a Silent Shadow; 36-70 an unknown contact worth checking; 71-00 something odd that may be nothing. The weight is printed 279 1bs, read as pounds.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.149-151'),
  ('ng-x40-storm-hammer', 'Storm Hammer Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 40 mph (64 km) maximum, at 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 10 ft (3 m) high or across, +30% with a running start; no thrusters for assisted leaps. Safe drops to 60 ft (18.3 m); from 60 to 120 ft (36.6 m) roll 1D20, on 1-10 the suit takes 2D4x10 M.D., the wearer 6D6 S.D.C./Hit Points and is stunned 1D4 melee rounds, on 11-20 the suit takes 5D6 M.D., the pilot 2D6 S.D.C. and loses two melee actions; higher drops do double the worse result and may kill.', 'None.', 'Cannot swim; walks the bottom at 4 mph (6.4 km/3.4 knots). Maximum depth 500 ft (152 m).', 'Man-sized: height 6-8 ft (1.8 to 2.4 m); width 4-5 ft (1.2 to 1.5 m); length 3.5-4 ft (1 to 1.2 m), all by the buyer''s size', '875 lbs (394 kg)', 200, 1, NULL, 1400000, '1.8 million credits nuclear, 1.4 million Solid Oxide; the lowest is stored. No electric version, too weak for its weapons.', 'Model Type: NG-X40. Class: Heavy Assault and Troop Support Power Armor. A one-man mobile artillery and anti-armor suit, meant to take on enemy suits, combat cyborgs, armored vehicles and giant robots or monsters from among the infantry, designed by a team led by Douglas Rood, Joshua Hill, Lawrence Scarlet and Chas Werltonal, who traded speed and versatility for firepower. A weapon cowl on its back carries a turreted particle beam cannon and the ammo drum for the rail gun that swallows the right forearm and hand; shoulder mini-missile launchers add reach. The cowl makes it top-heavy and a poor leaper. It is a heavy unit for cracking bunkers, light fortifications and armored formations. Destroying the cowl knocks out the turret and the rail gun, its drum gone with it. Robot P.S. 30. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 10 year supply, or Solid Oxide. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352), Robot P.S. 30: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Features beyond the standard: two simple helmet cameras storing 96 hours of video and 4,000 stills; a helmet language translator; passive nightvision (1,600 ft/488 m) with infrared optics (1,600 ft/488 m) and ultraviolet vision; and a binocular telescopic sight (2 miles/3.2 km).', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.151-153'),
  ('ng-dx001-thunder-hound', 'Thunder Hound Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (144 km) maximum, at 10% of the normal fatigue rate for Dog Boys; a human tires at 20% at high speed, 10% at 50 mph (80 km) or less. Leaping: 20 ft (6.1 m) high or across unassisted, jet-assisted 60 ft (18.3 m) high or across, each +50% with a running start (+30% for humans); the leg jets give straight up-and-down leaps to rooftops or onto big monsters. No power jumping.', 'None; it cannot even hover. Safe drops to 200 ft (61 m) on its back and leg thrusters; from 200 to 400 ft (122 m) roll 1D20, on 1-10 the suit takes 4D6 M.D. and the wearer loses 1D4 melee actions, on 11-20 no harm or delay; higher drops do 2D6x10 M.D. to the suit, 1D4x10 S.D.C./Hit Points to the wearer and stun him 1D4 melee rounds.', 'Not built for water; swims 12 mph (19 km/10.3 knots) or walks the bottom at 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots), at 10% of the normal fatigue rate for Dog Boys, 20% for humans. Maximum depth 500 ft (152 m).', 'Man-sized: height 5.6-8 ft (1.7 to 2.4 m); width 3-4 ft (0.9 to 1.2 m); length 2-4 ft (0.6 to 1.2 m), all by the wearer''s size', '440 lbs (198 kg)', 185, 1, NULL, 340000, '975,000 credits nuclear, 650,000 Solid Oxide, 340,000 electric battery; the lowest is stored. The HX-002 human model, with forearm weapons and extra optics and sensors, is 200,000 more; the DBX-003 for D-Bees is 250,000-500,000 more for fitting the armor to a nonhuman body (the model line says a flat 250,000). An NG energy pistol and an NG laser or ion rifle come as standard gear.', 'Model Type: NG DX-001 (Dog Boy); HX-002 (human) and DBX-003 (D-Bee) variants. Class: Armored Infantry Assault Suit. Power armor built for Dog Boys, the Coalition''s engineered canine soldiers. The idea began with a CS project to give its Psi-Hounds better armor; the CS shelved it, unsure that non-humans should hold that much power, and an NG team led by Cassandra Burke, Lee Carroll, Derek Japser and William Bailey kept going, altered the look enough to stand apart from the CS proposal while keeping a trace of the Dead Boy skull styling, and markets it as a junior partner to the NG-V61 Gunwolf robot. Since Dog Boys are never taught to pilot power armor, the DX-001 is simple and intuitive, little more than full environmental armor on a strength-boosting exoskeleton that lets the wearer run faster and leap farther. The helmet opens at the jaw like a clamshell, or comes off, so the Dog Boy can use his own senses, smell and psionics, and many keep it open until a fight starts. Beyond a retractable Vibro-Blade and a UEL in each forearm it has no built-in weapons and few extra sensors. Free and rogue Dog Boys know of it, but few can afford one, and the human HX-002 outsells it six to one. NG publicly denies making D-Bee versions and blames the Black Market, a lie told to keep the Coalition calm: it does build the customized DBX-003 for feline humanoids, Grackle-Tooths and others. The HX-002 is the same suit with a smaller, lower-mounted wolf helmet, an energy weapon on each forearm (20 M.D.C. each) and extra optics and sensors; aftermarket Techno-Wizard or magic weapons may replace its forearm weapons or be carried, though NG does not endorse them. Robot P.S. 28. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are priced. Handheld weapons: an NG energy pistol and laser or ion rifle are standard, and a Vibro-Sword, Neural Mace, shotgun, grenades or flares, monster-hunting gear, stakes and mallet (its own hand can drive a stake), magic items or other gear go on one or two belts, in a bag or backpack, or slung by a strap. UEL (2, one under plating in each forearm): a cable and E-Clip connector that powers a weapon of up to 1D6x10 M.D. an attack. Hand to hand: a Dog Boy keeps his usual bonuses and gains +1 attack per melee round and +1 each on initiative, strike, parry, dodge, disarm and roll with impact; one who has learned Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352) uses that skill''s bonuses instead. Robot P.S. 28: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Sensors: the DX-001 has the standard set only; the HX-002 adds two simple helmet cameras (96 hours of video, 4,000 stills), a language translator, passive nightvision (1,600 ft/488 m) with infrared (1,600 ft/488 m) and ultraviolet vision, and a binocular telescopic sight (2 miles/3.2 km).', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.154-156');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicle_locations (vehicle_slug, location, mdc, mdc_note, ordinal) VALUES
